Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Stitch Projection P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 635901e5-7a05-40a7-b855-664c9fa9ad49
@ [canonical_uuid] fc3a2e9e-1fc5-4b04-a867-431c2ab0584f

& [Problem]
  + verified repository candidate selection and compiled stitch projection are individually complete but cannot compose through a typed governed contract

& [Decision]
  + add one pure selected-only adapter that validates RSO evidence then constructs and verifies the already-defined stitch request

& [WhyNow]
  + it is the first missing dependency after RSO closure and turns repository-grounded lookahead from a selection receipt into an inference-host-consumable packet without requiring provider availability

& [Rejected]
  + modify RSO to emit stitches because that would broaden a closed signed observer
  + modify the stitch compiler to read repositories because that would mix semantic lifecycle with physical I O
  + invoke a model or optimize prompt placement because no provider performance or delivery contract is authorized

& [Consequence]
  + Cantor gains an auditable end-to-end provider-free path from exact repository bytes through selected terms to a compiled lifecycle projection while every runtime effect remains separate
